{"name":"Lollipop","hex":"#d91e3f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lollipop","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An item of confectionery consisting of a piece of candy or sweet attached to a stick.","Something having the shape of a lollipop: a linear stem connected to a round body."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To prune the lower branches of a tree or other plant so that new growth appears only at the top, where more light is received."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lollipop"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lollipop","blocks":[{"text":"A lollipop is a type of sugar candy usually consisting of hard candy mounted on a stick and intended for sucking or licking. Different informal terms are used in different places, including lolly and sucker. Lollipops are available in many flavors and shapes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Farbenfrohe_Lollipops%2C_Austria.jpg/330px-Farbenfrohe_Lollipops%2C_Austria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lollipop","wikidata":"Q217446"},{"title":"Lollipop (Lil Wayne song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Lollipop\" is a song by American rapper and singer Lil Wayne posthumously featuring fellow American singer Static Major. A dirty rap song with hip house, trap and R&B elements, it was released on March 13, 2008 as the lead single from the former's sixth studio album Tha Carter III. The track, which heavily utilizes the Auto-Tune vocal effect, was produced by American record producers Deezle and Jim Jonsin and features lyrics about sexual desire and oral sex. A remixed version with a guest appearance from American rapper Kanye West, as well as featuring new verses from Lil Wayne, was released as a bonus track for the album on iTunes."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/18/Lil_Wayne_-_Lollipop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lollipop_(Lil_Wayne_song)","wikidata":"Q2474196"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Rainbow-spiral_lollipop.JPG/500px-Rainbow-spiral_lollipop.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Rainbow-spiral_lollipop.JPG/1280px-Rainbow-spiral_lollipop.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Rainbow-spiral_lollipop.JPG/500px-Rainbow-spiral_lollipop.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spiral type with multi-color","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARainbow-spiral_lollipop.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Tootsie-Roll-Pop-Orange.jpg/500px-Tootsie-Roll-Pop-Orange.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Tootsie-Roll-Pop-Orange.jpg/1280px-Tootsie-Roll-Pop-Orange.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Tootsie-Roll-Pop-Orange.jpg/500px-Tootsie-Roll-Pop-Orange.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Tootsie Pop","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATootsie-Roll-Pop-Orange.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9d/LollipopScreen.JPG/330px-LollipopScreen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9d/LollipopScreen.JPG/330px-LollipopScreen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lil Wayne in the music video for \"Lollipop.\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALollipopScreen.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://upload.w